      "result": {
        "reply_text": "The District Commission shall not admit a complaint unless it is filed within two years from the date on which the cause of action has arisen, though a complaint may be entertained after this period if you satisfy the Commission that you had sufficient cause for not filing it within such period and the Commission records its reasons for condoning the delay.\n\nYou can seek guidance and lodge a grievance online through the National Consumer Helpline at https://consumerhelpline.gov.in/ or call their toll-free numbers 1915 or 1800-11-4000.\n\nYou may also file a consumer complaint electronically before the District Commission through the e-Jagriti portal at https://e-jagriti.gov.in/.\n\nKeep your receipts, payment proofs, and any communication with the repair shop ready.\n\nDo you have any receipts or proof of payment?\n\nHave you contacted the shop since the payment?\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 69\nSource: Department of Consumer Affairs - National Consumer Helpline (NCH), H NCH\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- I left out one point because I could not match it exactly to the official text. A lawyer or legal aid office can confirm it.\n\nBecause of the points above, please talk to a real lawyer or free legal aid office. (the event may be old enough that time limits could be a problem)\n\nFor free help from a real lawyer or legal aid office:\n- National Legal Services Authority Helpline: 15100 (Source: https://nalsa.gov.in/contact-us/)\n- Uttar Pradesh State Legal Services Authority Contact and Helpline: 1800-419-0234 / 0522-2286395 / 0522-2287972 (Source: http://uttarpradesh.nalsa.gov.in/contact-us/)\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
